<body>

<header>
  <h1>Why Is the Sky Blue?<span class="zh">为什么天空是蓝色的？</span></h1>
  <p class="sub">Three explanations · 三种解释</p>
</header>

<nav class="tabs" id="tabs">
  <button class="active" data-target="toddler">🧒 Toddler / 小朋友</button>
  <button data-target="teen">🎒 High School / 中学生</button>
  <button data-target="phd">🎓 PhD / 物理学博士</button>
</nav>

<main class="container">

  <!-- ─── Toddler ─── -->
  <div class="section active" id="sec-toddler">
    <div class="col">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-label"><span class="dot toddler"></span>English</div>
        <h2>🧒 For a 3-Year-Old Toddler</h2>
        <p>Sunlight looks white, but it's actually made of <strong>lots of rainbow colors mixed together</strong> — red, orange, yellow, green, blue, and purple!</p>
        <p>When sunlight travels all the way from the Sun to Earth, it has to pass through a big blanket of air called the <strong>atmosphere</strong>. That blanket is full of tiny, tiny particles — even smaller than a grain of sand!</p>
        <p>The blue color is bouncy. It bounces off all those tiny particles and spreads all around the sky. When you look up, that bouncing blue light is what you see. The red and yellow colors are less bouncy, so they just keep going straight through.</p>
        <p><strong>That's why the sky looks blue!</strong> 🌈💙</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-label"><span class="dot toddler"></span>中文</div>
        <h2>🧒 给三岁小朋友</h2>
        <p>阳光看起来是白色的，但实际上它是由<strong>很多彩虹颜色混合在一起</strong>组成的——红色、橙色、黄色、绿色、蓝色和紫色！</p>
        <p>当阳光从太阳一路旅行到地球时，它必须穿过一层厚厚的空气毯子，叫做<strong>大气层</strong>。这层空气毯子里充满了非常非常小的微粒——比一粒沙子还要小得多！</p>
        <p>蓝色光很爱弹跳。它会撞到那些小微粒，然后弹得到处都是，扩散到整个天空。当你抬头看时，你看到的就是那些弹跳的蓝光。红色和黄色的光不太爱弹跳，所以它们只是直接穿过去。</p>
        <p><strong>这就是天空看起来是蓝色的原因！</strong> 🌈💙</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ─── Teen ─── -->
  <div class="section" id="sec-teen">
    <div class="col">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-label"><span class="dot teen"></span>English</div>
        <h2>🎒 For a High School Student</h2>
        <p>Sunlight may look white, but it's actually a mixture of all visible wavelengths of light — from red (~700 nm) to violet (~400 nm). When this light enters Earth's atmosphere, it collides with gas molecules (mostly nitrogen and oxygen) and tiny particles.</p>
        <p>Here's where <strong>Rayleigh scattering</strong> comes in:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Molecules in the atmosphere are much smaller than the wavelength of visible light.</li>
          <li>Shorter wavelengths (blue and violet) scatter <strong>much more strongly</strong> than longer wavelengths (red and orange).</li>
          <li>The scattering intensity is proportional to <strong>1/λ⁴</strong> — meaning blue light (shorter wavelength) scatters roughly <strong>10× more</strong> than red light.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>So blue light gets scattered in all directions, and no matter where you look in the sky, scattered blue light reaches your eyes.</p>
        <p><strong>But wait — if violet scatters even more than blue, why isn't the sky violet?</strong> Three reasons:</p>
        <ol>
          <li>The Sun emits more blue light than violet light.</li>
          <li>Our eyes are much more sensitive to blue than violet.</li>
          <li>Some violet light is absorbed by the upper atmosphere.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-label"><span class="dot teen"></span>中文</div>
        <h2>🎒 给中学生</h2>
        <p>阳光看起来是白色的，但它实际上是由所有可见光波长混合而成的——从红色光（约 700 nm）到紫色光（约 400 nm）。当这些光线进入地球的大气层时，它们会与气体分子（主要是氮气和氧气）以及微小颗粒发生碰撞。</p>
        <p>这里就引入了<strong>瑞利散射</strong>：</p>
        <ul>
          <li>大气中的分子比可见光的波长小得多。</li>
          <li>较短的波长（蓝色和紫色）比较长的波长（红色和橙色）<strong>散射得强烈得多</strong>。</li>
          <li>散射强度与 <strong>1/λ⁴</strong> 成正比——这意味着蓝光（波长较短）的散射强度大约是红光（波长较长）的 <strong>10 倍</strong>。</li>
        </ul>
        <p>因此，蓝光向各个方向散射，无论你望向天空的哪个方向，散射的蓝光都会进入你的眼睛。</p>
        <p><strong>但是等等——如果紫光的散射比蓝光还强，那天空为什么不是紫色的呢？</strong> 原因有三：</p>
        <ol>
          <li>太阳发出的蓝光比紫光多。</li>
          <li>人眼对蓝色的敏感度远高于紫色。</li>
          <li>部分紫光被高层大气吸收了。</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ─── PhD ─── -->
  <div class="section" id="sec-phd">
    <div class="col">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-label"><span class="dot phd"></span>English</div>
        <h2>🎓 For a Physics PhD</h2>
        <p>The blue color of the sky is a consequence of <strong>Rayleigh scattering</strong> — the elastic scattering of electromagnetic radiation by particles much smaller than the incident wavelength. Formally, we treat atmospheric molecules (N₂, O₂) as induced dipole oscillators in the electric field of the incoming photon.</p>

        <h3>Scattering Cross Section</h3>
        <p>For a particle of radius <em>a</em> ≪ λ, the differential scattering cross section per molecule is:</p>
        <div class="math">dσ/dΩ = 2π⁵α² / (3λ⁴) · (1 + cos²θ)</div>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>α</strong> is the molecular polarizability</li>
          <li><strong>θ</strong> is the scattering angle</li>
          <li>The <strong>1/λ⁴</strong> dependence is the hallmark of Rayleigh scattering</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Spectral Scattering &amp; Attenuation</h3>
        <div class="math">σ<sub>scat</sub>(λ) ∝ (n² − 1) / (λ⁴N)</div>
        <p>where <em>n</em> is the refractive index and <em>N</em> is the molecular number density. At 450 nm (blue), σ ≈ 5×10⁻³¹ cm², while at 650 nm (red), σ ≈ 5×10⁻³² cm² — roughly an order of magnitude difference.</p>

        <h3>Why Not Violet?</h3>
        <p>Despite violet light (~400 nm) scattering ~2.4× more than blue (~475 nm), the sky appears blue due to the convolution of:</p>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Solar spectral irradiance</strong> — which drops in the UV/violet (AM1.5 spectrum peaks ~500 nm)</li>
          <li><strong>CIE photopic luminosity function</strong> — human cone response (S-cones peak ~420 nm but overall sensitivity is low; M- and L-cones respond more strongly to blue-green)</li>
          <li><strong>Ozone absorption</strong> — the Hartley and Huggins bands attenuate UV and near-UV violet light in the stratosphere</li>
        </ol>

        <h3>Beyond Rayleigh</h3>
        <p>For completeness, in polluted or humid conditions, <strong>Mie scattering</strong> (particles with size comparable to λ) becomes relevant. Mie scattering is nearly wavelength-independent and produces the white-gray appearance of haze or clouds. The transition between Rayleigh-dominated and Mie-dominated regimes is governed by the size parameter <em>x = 2πa/λ</em>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-label"><span class="dot phd"></span>中文</div>
        <h2>🎓 给物理学博士</h2>
        <p>天空的蓝色是<strong>瑞利散射</strong>的结果——即电磁辐射被远小于入射波长的粒子发生的弹性散射。严格来说，我们将大气分子（N₂、O₂）视为入射光子电场中的感应偶极子振荡器。</p>

        <h3>散射截面</h3>
        <p>对于半径 <em>a</em> ≪ λ 的粒子，每个分子的微分散射截面为：</p>
        <div class="math">dσ/dΩ = 2π⁵α² / (3λ⁴) · (1 + cos²θ)</div>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>α</strong> 为分子极化率</li>
          <li><strong>θ</strong> 为散射角</li>
          <li><strong>1/λ⁴</strong> 的依赖关系是瑞利散射的标志性特征</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>谱散射与衰减</h3>
        <div class="math">σ<sub>scat</sub>(λ) ∝ (n² − 1) / (λ⁴N)</div>
        <p>其中 <em>n</em> 为折射率，<em>N</em> 为分子数密度。在 450 nm（蓝光）处，σ ≈ 5×10⁻³¹ cm²；而在 650 nm（红光）处，σ ≈ 5×10⁻³² cm²——相差约一个数量级。</p>

        <h3>为什么不是紫色？</h3>
        <p>尽管紫光（约 400 nm）的散射强度约为蓝光（约 475 nm）的 2.4 倍，但天空呈现蓝色，这是因为以下几个因素的综合结果：</p>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>太阳光谱辐照度</strong>——在紫外/紫光区域下降（AM1.5 光谱峰值约在 500 nm）</li>
          <li><strong>CIE 明视觉光谱光视效率函数</strong>——人眼视锥细胞响应（S 视锥细胞峰值约在 420 nm，但整体敏感度较低；M 视锥和 L 视锥对蓝绿光的响应更强）</li>
          <li><strong>臭氧吸收</strong>——哈特利吸收带和哈金斯吸收带在平流层中衰减了紫外和近紫外紫光</li>
        </ol>

        <h3>超越瑞利散射</h3>
        <p>为完备起见，在污染或潮湿条件下，<strong>米氏散射</strong>（粒子尺寸与 λ 相当）变得重要。米氏散射几乎与波长无关，产生雾霾或云层的白灰色外观。瑞利散射主导和米氏散射主导之间的转换由尺寸参数 <em>x = 2πa/λ</em> 控制。</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="epilogue">
    The sky is blue because the universe happens to provide a Sun with a blackbody spectrum, an atmosphere with small molecules, and eyes with just the right sensitivity — all aligned to paint our skies in cerulean.<br>
    天空之所以是蓝色的，是因为宇宙恰好给了我们一颗具有黑体辐射光谱的太阳、一个充满小分子的大气层，以及一双敏感度刚刚好的眼睛——所有条件都恰到好处，将我们的天空染成了天蓝色。
  </p>
</main>

<script>
(function(){
  const tabs = document.getElementById('tabs');
  const btns = tabs.querySelectorAll('button');
  btns.forEach(function(btn){
    btn.addEventListener('click',function(){
      btns.forEach(function(b){b.classList.remove('active')});
      btn.classList.add('active');
      document.querySelectorAll('.section').forEach(function(s){s.classList.remove('active')});
      document.getElementById('sec-'+btn.dataset.target).classList.add('active');
    });
  });
})();
</script>
</body>
</html>
